<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="A sanitized home-server infrastructure case study."><title>Hardware · Home Server</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css"></head><body><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="../index.html" aria-label="Engineering Notebook home"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 4h6v6H4zM14 4h6v6h-6zM4 14h6v6H4zM14 14h6v6h-6z"/></svg><span class="nav-label">Engineering Notebook</span></a><nav aria-label="Home-server navigation"><div class="home-server-links"><a href="/home-server/">Overview</a><a class="active" href="/home-server/hardware/">Hardware</a><a href="/home-server/security/">Security</a><a href="/home-server/monitoring/">Monitoring</a><a href="/home-server/backups/">Backups</a><a href="/home-server/services/">Services</a><a href="/home-server/lessons/">Lessons</a></div><a href="/projects/"><span class="nav-label">← Projects</span></a></nav></header><main><section class="intro section-shell"><p class="eyebrow">HOME SERVER / HARDWARE</p><h1>Hardware</h1><p class="lede">The machine started as a pile of parts, a screwdriver, and more confidence than evidence.</p><button class="intro-scroll-cue" type="button" aria-label="Scroll to next section"></button></section><section class="section-shell"><div class="feature-card"><div class="card-kicker">THE BUILD</div><h3>Model-level details are enough for the public story.</h3><p>The system uses an AMD Ryzen 9 9900X processor, 32 GB of DDR5 memory, a 2 TB NVMe SSD, an ASUS ROG Strix X870-I Gaming WiFi motherboard, a compact case, and a CyberPower UPS.</p><p>The public page shows the complete original frames at their original dimensions. Opaque masks permanently cover drive serials, PSIDs, barcodes, installer device names, and other unique identifiers.</p></div></section><section class="section-shell"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">WHAT WENT WRONG</p><h2>The first boot was a negotiation.</h2></div><div class="note-grid"><article class="note-card"><span>01</span><h3>Firmware surprises</h3><p>Replacing the CPU triggered firmware and TPM questions. The recovery path had to be understood before pressing the tempting button.</p></article><article class="note-card"><span>02</span><h3>Hardware detective work</h3><p>Bluetooth and wireless hardware needed additional driver work. The external antenna turned out to be less decorative than it looked.</p></article><article class="note-card"><span>03</span><h3>Storage layout</h3><p>The large disk was installed with EFI, boot, and an LVM-backed root volume so storage could be extended later.</p></article></div></section><section class="section-shell"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">BUILD PHOTOS</p><h2>The public gallery uses sanitized copies.</h2></div><div class="photo-grid"><figure><img src="../images/public/00D3AEEC-4955-4189-B66C-A7F09714784C_1_105_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>Firmware setup: the machine introducing itself before the operating system gets a vote.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/1AE80B23-8689-4CC0-B268-12F076C0285C_4_5005_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>A firmware update in the middle of the build story.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/1B26E1A8-35A0-451A-B1D9-CACE088CB35A_1_102_o.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>The parts pile, with the lower identifier area permanently masked.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/1DEFD7EC-CAF1-4AEB-923D-B6392E6DE2BE_4_5005_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>The case and its growing collection of cables.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/231B5E16-907D-44D3-ADFD-4AEB72108621_1_102_o.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>Motherboard close-up, with component identifiers masked.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/2597013A-DA11-4B61-8F95-3B866A7F05B1_1_105_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>A small hardware detail from the assembly.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/25F82E47-DF0A-40E6-8D98-6E665C07D50A_1_105_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>Another angle from the parts bench.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/273F10FE-3DC6-43AE-B30D-76F8EB16A772_1_105_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>A break from debugging; screen content is permanently masked.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/3202610B-1BF2-4966-8972-F0A0907C4D6D_1_105_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>Storage layout during installation, with device identifiers masked.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/3F1D41A3-57EF-4BAB-B8DD-B5761C0B0BC0_4_5005_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>A component label photographed during the build.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/436C6D13-B5F6-49D4-BB3C-94008A7BF65F_1_105_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>Cooling: because processors also prefer not to panic.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/492E2158-2721-4EEE-997D-C93D794E0E13_1_105_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>Drive packaging with barcode information permanently masked.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/67CAC70D-0802-42E7-BF37-81B46ACFE515_1_105_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>Storage hardware before installation; unique labels are masked.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/7B4F3CC2-13FF-4A11-96A5-C3D03E4CE6D2_1_102_o.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>Parts on the table before the first successful boot.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/808E4B86-C569-4ACC-81F3-00E861725EB2_1_105_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>The first boot: enough information to confirm the parts, and enough warnings to make coffee.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/813817C0-64A6-4A0B-9C73-8845A8429E75_1_105_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>Writing installation media, with local device details masked.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/820A4A59-8959-4FC8-AE84-BA1F24CC9181_1_105_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>A connector close-up from the hardware workbench.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/A14929D6-D966-4B03-B7D0-13F71018D91E_1_105_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>The case after the parts began cooperating.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/AD8C67B3-8366-44AD-AEAB-31D943D79E1B_1_105_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>Firmware readings during the first boot.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/BB8ECD2F-08EB-4137-829F-8623231B442D_1_105_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>Another firmware checkpoint before installation.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/CDEC2AF8-BC54-488E-ACF3-C174C806E47D_1_201_a.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>A full-size build detail, re-encoded without photo metadata.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/E6893234-DEE4-4B38-A6CF-FBC7080DC3C5_1_105_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>Drive model detail with the unique label area permanently masked.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/EC7E4302-882F-4823-9AC9-ADA18402E011_1_102_o.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>A compact case, a new motherboard, and a suspicious number of cables.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="../images/public/F757F4DC-C5CA-41FC-84D8-827105A79F6A_1_105_c.jpg" alt="Home-server build photo"><figcaption>Installing Ubuntu, with one failed target to keep the story honest.</figcaption></figure></div></section></main><script is:inline src="../../scroll-cue.js"></script></body></html>